System Reference Document 5.1
-----------------------------

The rules content in backend/internal/rules/srd51 (races, classes, features,
spells, equipment, creatures and their descriptions) comes from the System
Reference Document 5.1. The app shows the same attribution on its credits
page.

This work includes material taken from the System Reference Document 5.1 ("SRD 5.1") by Wizards of the Coast LLC and available at https://dnd.wizards.com/resources/systems-reference-document. The SRD 5.1 is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License available at https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.

Changes: the SRD 5.1 material was converted to structured JSON, and we added
Portuguese names and structured rule effects written by us.


System Reference Document 5.2.1
-------------------------------

Three tables of the System Reference Document 5.2.1 (the 2024 rules) are used:

- The ways of making ability scores in the table's rules (RN-24: the standard
  array, the 27-point buy and "4d6, drop the lowest", p. 20 of the SRD 5.2.1),
  in backend/internal/rules/abilitymethods.go.
- The "XP Budget per Character" table (p. 201): the XP a party spends at each
  level in a low, moderate or high encounter, in
  backend/internal/rules/srd51/effects/encounter_budget.json, used by the
  encounter builder (backend/internal/rules/encounter).
- The "Magic Item Rarities and Values" table (p. 205: common 100 GP, uncommon
  400, rare 4,000, very rare 40,000, legendary 200,000; an artifact is
  priceless; a consumable is worth half), in
  backend/internal/rules/srd51/effects/magic_item_values.json, used by the
  treasure generator.

The app labels each one "SRD 5.2.1 (regras de 2024)".

